@identityHost = http://localhost:8080
@transactionHost = http://localhost:8084
@email = transaction@example.com
@password = Transaction123!
@transactionId = 77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777
@customerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@sourceWalletId = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@destinationWalletId = 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555
@accessToken = paste-access-token-here

### Service information
GET {{transactionHost}}/
Accept: application/json

### Liveness check
GET {{transactionHost}}/health/live
Accept: application/json

### Readiness check (SQL Server and messaging provider)
GET {{transactionHost}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

### Register an Identity user
POST {{identityHost}}/api/identity-users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Get a Transaction access token, then copy access_token above
POST {{identityHost}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=vault-swagger&client_secret=vault-swagger-secret&grant_type=password&username={{email}}&password={{password}}&scope=vault.transaction.api

### Create transfer; RabbitMQ saga should move it to Completed
POST {{transactionHost}}/api/transactions/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "{{transactionId}}",
  "initiatingCustomerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "sourceWalletId": "{{sourceWalletId}}",
  "destinationWalletId": "{{destinationWalletId}}",
  "currency": "TRY",
  "amount": 42.50,
  "reference": "rabbitmq-saga"
}

### Get transaction
GET {{transactionHost}}/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Get transactions by customer
GET {{transactionHost}}/api/transactions/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json
